{title: Sundown}
{artist: Gordon Lightfoot}
{key: E}
{duration: 3:00}
{tempo: 106}


{start_of_part: Intro}
[E5]
{end_of_part}


{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
I can [E5]see her lyin' back
In her satin dress
In a [B7sus4]room  where you do
What you [E5]don't confess
{end_of_verse}


{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[E5]  Sundown you'd [A]better take care
If I [D]find you been creepin' 'round
[E5]My back stairs
Sundown you'd [A]better take care
If I [D]find you been creepin' 'round
[E5]My back stairs
{end_of_chorus}


{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
She's been [E5]lookin' like a queen
In a sailor's dream
And she [B7sus4]don't always say
What she [E5]really means
{end_of_verse}


{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[E5]  Sometimes I [A]think it's a shame
When I [D]get feelin' better
When I'm [E5]feelin' no pain
Sometimes I [A]think it's a shame
When I [D]get feelin' better
When I'm [E5]feelin' no pain
{end_of_chorus}


{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
I can [E5]picture every move
That a man could make
Getting [B7sus4]lost  in her lovin'
Is your [E5]first mistake
{end_of_verse}


{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[E5]  Sundown you'd [A]better take care
If I [D]find you been creepin' 'round
[E5]My back stairs
Sometimes I [A]think it's a sin
When I [D]feel like I'm winnin'
When I'm [E5]losin' again
{end_of_chorus}


